three major US cities are suing the  Pentagon for an alleged failure to tell  them when service members are  disqualified from owning a gun New York  City Philadelphia and San Francisco  filed that lawsuit yesterday they want  defense officials to openly report all  military criminal convictions David  Martin is at the Pentagon with the legal  action and the government responds David  good morning good morning the Defense  Department's mission is to protect the  United States but a lawsuit filed by  three big city mayors claims the  Pentagon's repeated failures to report  violent criminals to the FBI have  actually put the public in danger  the lawsuit stems from last month's  Texas church massacre by a former member  of the Air Force  Devon Kelly was able to buy the gun he  used to kill 26 worshippers and  Sutherland Springs just outside San  Antonio because the Air Force failed to  report his conviction for a domestic  assault to the FBI if the conviction had  been reported Kelly's name would have  been entered into the database of people  barred from purchasing firearms the Air  Force admitted it failed to report  several dozen other violent offenders as  well San Francisco city attorney Dennis  Herrera Belize Court intervention is  needed to make sure the Defense  Department does its job in the future  it's unfortunate that it took that  tragedy to highlight and bring out into  the mainstream what has been going on  for all too long and that is a  department offense his failure to live  up to its responsibilities according to  the lawsuit filed by the Democratic  mayors of New York Philadelphia and San  Francisco a 2017 Defense Department  study revealed the Air Force failed to  submit final reports in about 14% of  cases the Navy and Marines in about 36%  of cases and the Army in about 41%  Pentagon's Inspector General told  Congress earlier this month such  failures were long-running and  widespread among all the armed services  inadequate training inadequate  verification they didn't take these  recommendations as seriously as they  should have  the Pentagon has promised to fix the  problem but the lawsuit asks the judge  to compel the military to go back over  all cases and report all the violent  offenders it failed to report to the FBI  the first time the Justice Department is  reviewing the lawsuit to determine its  next step Dana  David Martin at the Pentagon David thank  you
 

